\title{Feast of the Transfiguration 2026}
\tag{cmc}
\date{2026-08-09}
\author{liamoc}
\quote{
  Tibi dixit cor meum, quæsívi vultum tuum, vultum tuum Dómine requíram: ne avértas fáciem tuam a me.
}
\p{I was once again the director of our choir at [All Saints Ainslie](https://allsaintsainslie.org.au), on a cold and wet Sunday with few choristers and few parishioners, even though it was a transferred feast. We sang Stopford's [Do not be afraid](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8aNISuvsP5M), a poem by Gerard Markland based on the words of Isaiah:}
\quote{
  \poem{
    \line{Do not be afraid, for I have redeemed you.}
    \line{I have called you by your name;}
    \line{you are mine.}
    \line{When you walk through the waters,}
    \line{I'll be with you;}
    \line{you will never sink beneath the waves.}
    \line{When the fire is burning all around you,}
    \line{you will never be consumed by the flames.}
    \line{When the fear of loneliness is looming,}
    \line{then remember I am at your side.}
    \line{When you dwell in the exile of a stranger,}
    \line{remember you are precious in my eyes.}
    \line{You are mine, O my child,}
    \line{I am your Father,}
    \line{and I love you with a perfect love.}
    \line{Do not be afraid, for I have redeemed you.}
    \line{I have called you by your name;}
    \line{you are mine.}
  }
}
\p{There's something weird going on, because we celebrated the Transfiguration already on [Quinquagesima Sunday](loc-0038), and last year they made no special observance of the feast of the Transfiguration. The transferring of feasts is such a mess! I'm liking [[obrw]]'s policy of never transferring anything and celebrating feasts on the day more and more.}